# Update pill on the phone, built to the approved cards soma-chat/Updates (Boss approved all six, 2026-10-29).
# canvas-app: soma-chat
# Isolated fictional offers in the preview app (UpdatesPreview): nothing installs, a tap only moves the fixture on.
# Look at each shot against its card: red pill before [ artifacts · N ]; the sheet's Soma panel with its checks line
# (green signed/walks, accent design line), the app that couldn't update by itself, the "Updated by themselves"
# history; on the cover everything that needs a tap on the first screen. The states card is a catalog of four states:
# the four state shots are looked at against it by eye (one real screen shows one state at a time).
fold folded
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -W -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --es updates offer
expect Updates · 2
expect artifacts
shot update-pill-cover card=soma-update-pill-cover
tap Updates · 2
expect What changed
expect update and restart Soma
expect taken and signed for this phone
expect not approved yet
expect didn’t update by itself: Android asked for a confirmation
expect update Soma Messages
absent update Hunch
shot update-sheet-cover card=soma-update-sheet-cover
scrollto Soma updates only when you tap
expect Hunch 0.7.2 → 0.7.3
expect Soma updates only when you tap
clearlog
tap update Soma Messages
log fixture update tap dev.omalauncher.messages
absent update Soma Messages
clearlog
tap update and restart Soma
log fixture update tap dev.omalauncher.boss
expect Waits for Phone B
shot update-state-waiting-cover
tap cancel
log fixture update cancel
expect update and restart Soma
key BACK
wait 1500
absent Updated by themselves
expect Update Soma · 176
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -W -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --es updates updating
tap updating
expect Android restarts Soma
expect check the signature and version
shot update-state-updating-cover
key BACK
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -W -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --es updates updated
tap updated
expect Soma 176 is running. 6 phone checks wait for us
shot update-state-updated-cover
tap later
wait 1500
absent Updated by themselves
absent updated
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -W -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --es updates failed
tap didn’t update
expect Kept 175: Android refused the package
expect try again
expect copy details for an agent
shot update-state-failed-cover
key BACK
fold unfolded
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -W -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --es updates offer
expect Updates · 2
shot update-pill-unfolded card=soma-update-pill-unfolded
tap Updates · 2
expect What changed
expect update and restart Soma
expect update Soma Messages
expect Updated by themselves
shot update-sheet-unfolded card=soma-update-sheet-unfolded
key BACK
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -W -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --es updates waiting
tap waiting
expect Waits for Phone B
shot update-state-waiting-unfolded
key BACK
[phone] After the next bundle is installed: an offer written by oma-offer for a real Hunch, Soma Notes or Soma Messages build updates by itself only while that app is closed (open it first: nothing happens until it is closed), lands in "Updated by themselves", and the app opens at the new version.
[phone] Say whether the silent PackageInstaller session still brings Play Protect's "install without scanning" prompt; if it does, the app must wait in the pill with that reason, never install behind it. Nothing in Soma touches Play Protect.
[phone] Soma's own offer: with an agent mid-turn, [ update and restart Soma ] shows Waiting with that agent's name; once idle it updates in place (Linux, logins, settings kept) and reopens on "Soma N is running" with the phone-check count; ~/.cache/oma-update/updated.json lists them.
[phone] A failed install (e.g. an APK not signed with this phone's key) keeps the old version and shows Didn't update with the reason and [ try again ].
